# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Everything here is OPTIONAL: the app's data
# sources (Darwin VAAC over BOM's public FTP, Open-Meteo wind, Esri basemap
# tiles) are all keyless, and the app runs fully without this file.

# Published NOTAMs for an aerodrome, shown under "Airports under ash".
#
# SkyLink sells the same data through two channels, which differ in base URL
# and auth header. Paste whichever key you hold; the channel is inferred from
# its shape, because sending one channel's key to the other returns a 403 that
# reads like a bug in this app.
#
#   Direct    a UUID licence key from SkyLink's own checkout (billed via Polar)
#             -> https://data.skylinkapi.com/v3.1, header x-api-key
#   RapidAPI  a long dashless key from the RapidAPI marketplace
#             -> https://skylink-api.p.rapidapi.com, header x-rapidapi-key
#             (the RapidAPI account must also be SUBSCRIBED to the SkyLink API;
#              a valid key alone returns "You are not subscribed to this API")
#
# Free tier is 1,000 requests/month, so /api/notams caches per ICAO for 10 min.
# Read server-side only; never sent to the browser. Unset, the lookup reports
# itself unconfigured and nothing else changes.
SKYLINK_API_KEY=

# Only needed to override the inferred channel: "direct" or "rapidapi".
# SKYLINK_API_CHANNEL=

# --- Durable bulletin cache (optional) --------------------------------------
#
# A published bulletin never changes, so it is downloaded once and cached. On a
# server that is enough. On serverless every cold start begins with an empty
# process and an empty filesystem, so a Redis layer is what keeps the
# "download each bulletin once" property.
#
# The same store also backs the per-IP rate limit on /api/* (proxy.ts). Without
# it the limit falls back to a per-instance counter, which on serverless only
# catches a flood that happens to land on one instance — fine for local and
# preview, not a real limit in production.
#
# NOTE: Vercel KV is deprecated — its stores moved to Upstash Redis, which is
# what the Vercel Marketplace provisions now (Storage -> Redis). The
# integration injects these for you; both naming schemes are accepted.
#
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
#
# Legacy names from the old Vercel KV integration also work:
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
